    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0246" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/395a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at La
                        Paz</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hazeltine</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-02T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 2,
                                1919, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>You are instructed to proceed immediately to Arica for the purpose of
                    confidentially investigating and cabling the Department a report on the present
                    treatment of Peruvians by the local Chilean authorities. After making such a
                    report you are directed to proceed to Iquique and to cable Department a similar
                    report from that place. While in Iquique you will also investigate the recent
                    departure of the Peruvian Consul, with a view to ascertaining whether or not it
                    was voluntary. In both of these places you will state that the purpose of your
                    visit is merely to confer with the American Consular Agents.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>You are instructed to take your code with you in order that your reports on the
                    above subject may be made in cipher.</p>
                <p>Remain in Iquique until you are instructed to return to La Paz.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
